  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226152/assets/fe0207214fb16ac0871e15f3be7c9fa33670a7df3617f5f9e0b92b45a09c76af.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $0<\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Further,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{4}{4})=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$",
